y well, takes responsibility seriously. Concerns: regarded as arrogant, relatively weak leadership, also arrogant.\n\nWe need to weigh criteria: reliability, stress resilience, technical competence, decision quality, attention, crew cooperation, communication, responsibility, adaptability.\n\nCandidate C: reliability high, decision quality high, crew cooperation positive, but communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). Could be a concern for long-distance flights requiring teamwork and continuous learning.\n\nCandidate B: stress resilience high, conscientious (reliability), good weather assessment (technical), computer skills, but uncooperative and grumpy (crew cooperation, communication). Could be problematic.\n\nCandidate A: anticipates danger (decision quality), sees complex connections (technical), spatial vision (technical), leadership (crew), but unorganized (reliability) and not good at criticism (adaptability). Might be okay but organization is important.\n\nCandidate D: problem solving, concentration, responsibility, handles unexpected events, but arrogant and weak leadership, also arrogance may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWhich is best overall? Hard. Maybe Candidate A has strong technical and leadership but organization issues. Candidate C has reliability and crew atmosphere but communication issues. Candidate B has stress resilience but uncooperative. Candidate D has responsibility but arrogance.\n\nProbably Candidate A might be best if organization can be managed. But we need evidence. Let's start by bringing up Candidate A's strengths and concerns, and propose provisional vote for A, but open to discussion.\n\nWe need to reference no prior discussion, but we can say \"I will start by discussing Candidate A\". Provide vote.\n\nProceed."}
